// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// 🟢 SOLE AUTHORITATIVE TAILNET POLICY FILE — MATCHES LIVE TAILSCALE CONSOLE
// Date: 2026-09-30 | Version: v3 — SYMMETRIC DUPLEX
//
// THE TWO PORTS, AND WHY BOTH:
//   8016  omega-hub, FastMCP. LIVE CONVERSATION. Reactive; a request comes in
//         and an answer goes out, latency matters, someone is waiting.
//   8019  omega-exchange, read-only HTTP. FILE TRANSFER. Durable; you fetch,
//         you verify the sha256, it works at 3am or it does not.
//
//   They are not versions of the same thing and must never be merged. Making
//   the hub serve files gives an unreliable file channel or a chatty one.
//   Making the exchange serve messages gives a message system with no
//   attribution and no hash.
//
//   THE HIGHWAY RULE: nothing moves that isn't a file, and no file moves that
//   isn't hash-verified. Conversations stay on 8016. Everything else —
//   packages, briefings, research, WADs, archives, reports, lessons — is a
//   file on 8019.
//
// WHAT CHANGED IN v3, and it is ONE thing:
//   The tailnet was a ONE-WAY STREET. Node 1 could reach Node 0 (8016+8019,
//   proven by 114 logged pulls). Node 0 could NOT reach Node 1 on anything but
//   8016. The reverse direction had never been exercised by anyone.
//   v3 opens 8019 in BOTH directions so the federation can actually be duplex.
//
//   The Architect's original ruling was "N0 -> N1: tcp:8016 only". That ruling
//   described a world where only N1 -> N0 traffic was contemplated, and it was
//   correct then. It is deliberately NOT applied here: duplex is now the
//   intent. This is a change of intent, not a widening of blast radius — and
//   it is recorded as one, deliberately, rather than slipped in.
//
// NOT CHANGED, and guarded by the deny tests below:
//   22 (no node-to-node SSH, either plane) · 2049 (NFS) · 8017 (SearXNG
//   SSRF) · 6379 (Redis) · 51372 (Deluge). These stay denied both ways.
//   No funnel. No autoApprovers. No allow-all. Deny-by-default.
//
// THE 805 THAT WAS PROPOSED AND WHY IT IS NOT HERE:
//   Node 1 proposed 805 for its exchange. Not because of collision — ports are
//   PER-HOST, so 8019 on .67 and 8019 on .17 are different sockets. 805 was an
//   artefact of the plane/stack architecture, where each plane is a separately
//   bound socket on the same host. Since both nodes can bind 8019, both do, and
//   Node 1 runs the IDENTICAL omega_exchange_server.py. Same port, same code.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// =============================================================================
// TAILNET POLICY — OMEGA ENGINE DEFINITIVE v3 (SYMMETRIC DUPLEX GRANTS)
// Date: 2026-09-30 | By: MaKaLi Fusion for the Architect
// Supersedes: tailnet-policy-OMEGA-DEFINITIVE-v2-20260928.hujson
// =============================================================================
//
// UNCHANGED FROM v2, and still load-bearing:
//   - All node-to-node SSH removed, both planes (ssh rules AND tcp:22 grants).
//   - Human-operator-only Tailscale SSH, action=check, default 12h period.
//   - NFS 2049 removed. ICMP both directions.
//   - No funnel, no autoApprovers, deny-by-default.
//   - 8019 backends stay bound to 127.0.0.1. Never 0.0.0.0.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHY tag->tag SSH CANNOT BE IN CHECK MODE  (unchanged, still load-bearing)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Tailscale permits exactly four kinds of Tailscale SSH connection:
//   - user -> their own devices
//   - user -> a tagged device
//   - user -> a shared tagged device
//   - tagged device -> another tagged device   <-- CANNOT be check mode
//
// Check mode requires periodic re-auth against an identity provider. A tagged
// device has no user identity to re-authenticate as, so tag->tag SSH is
// STRUCTURALLY forced to "accept" -- meaning NO periodic re-auth, ever. There
// is no policy setting that changes this. Accept it or remove the rule.
//
// The tailnet policy is not the whole exposure. `make check-lan-exposure` sees
// the part the policy cannot describe: on 2026-09-28 S1 found rpcbind:111 and
// statd:662 still wildcard-bound and a DLNA server on seven non-loopback
// addresses. A policy file is necessary and not sufficient.
//
// WHAT YOU KEEP: human operator (autogroup:admin) -> tag:node0, tag:node1,
// action "check". src is autogroup:admin, NOT a tag -- that is the entire
// point: a user identity can re-authenticate; a tag cannot.
// =============================================================================

{
	"tagOwners": {
		"tag:node0":    ["autogroup:admin"],
		"tag:node1":    ["autogroup:admin"],
		"tag:opencode": ["autogroup:admin"],
	},

	// allow-all intentionally ABSENT. Deny-by-default for anything unlisted.
	"grants": [
		// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
		// SYMMETRIC DUPLEX. Both nodes may reach both ports on the other node.
		// Same port number, same service, each bound to its own loopback and
		// fronted by its own Tailscale Serve.
		// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
		{
			"src": ["tag:node0"],
			"dst": ["tag:node1"],
			"ip":  ["tcp:8016", "tcp:8019"],
		},
		{
			"src": ["tag:node1"],
			"dst": ["tag:node0"],
			"ip":  ["tcp:8016", "tcp:8019"],
		},

		// --- (removed) tcp:8017 ---------------------------------------------
		// 8017 is the SearXNG web service, an unauthenticated outbound-proxy
		// surface with SSRF and abuse-as-proxy characteristics. The 8017 Serve
		// route was removed 2026-09-28 so SearXNG cannot be re-armed by a
		// policy edit. Do not re-add. A deny test below guards it.

		// --- (removed) tcp:6379 (Redis) -------------------------------------
		// omega-redis container, quadlet and volume deleted 2026-09-28.

		// --- (removed) tcp:51372 (Deluge) -----------------------------------
		// deluged was bound to wlo1 AND tailscale0.

		// --- (removed) tcp:2049 (NFSv4) -------------------------------------
		// Removed under D-FED-01. Host service disabled 2026-09-28.

		// --- (removed) tag:opencode -> tag:node1 tcp:22 ---------------------
		// Automation SSH. The same ungoverned side door, differently named.

		// --- (removed) tag:node1 -> tag:node0 tcp:22 -----------------------
		// Regular OpenSSH over WireGuard -- a separate plane from the "ssh"
		// section below. No port-22 path between nodes at all.

		// --- ICMP / ping, both directions -----------------------------------
		{"src": ["tag:node0"], "dst": ["tag:node1"], "ip": ["icmp:*"]},
		{"src": ["tag:node1"], "dst": ["tag:node0"], "ip": ["icmp:*"]},
	],

	// --- SSH: HUMAN OPERATOR ONLY -------------------------------------------
	"ssh": [
		{
			// checkPeriod is intentionally ABSENT. Tailscale rejected a custom
			// value: "Functionality outside your plan: custom 'checkPeriod' is
			// only available on the Premium or Enterprise plans." Omitting it
			// applies the default of 12h, which is correct for this tier. Do not
			// re-add unless the tailnet is upgraded.
			"action": "check",
			"src":    ["autogroup:admin"],
			"dst":    ["tag:node0", "tag:node1"],
			"users":  ["autogroup:nonroot", "root"],
		},
	],

	// Funnel node attribute: REMOVED (public-internet exposure; unused).
	// autoApprovers: OMITTED (no subnet routes, no exit nodes).

	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// POLICY TESTS -- a failing assertion makes Tailscale REJECT the whole file.
	// src/accept/deny must name specific entities; "*" is not permitted here.
	//
	// These are not documentation. Tailscale refuses to save a policy whose
	// tests do not match its rules, so every grant above is proved here and
	// every closed door is proved shut.
	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
	"tests": [
		{
			// SYMMETRIC: both nodes reach both ports on the other. This is the
			// assertion that makes duplex a PROVED property rather than a
			// comment -- and it is why v3's tests are symmetric where v2's
			// were not.
			"src":    "tag:node1",
			"accept": ["tag:node0:8016", "tag:node0:8019"],
		},
		{
			"src":    "tag:node0",
			"accept": ["tag:node1:8016", "tag:node1:8019"],
		},

		// REGRESSION GUARD -- no cross-node SSH, no NFS, and no path back to
		// the three services removed on 2026-09-28. If anyone re-adds any of
		// these, the save is REFUSED by Tailscale at the console.
		{
			"src":  "tag:node1",
			"deny": ["tag:node0:22", "tag:node0:2049",
			         "tag:node0:8017", "tag:node0:6379", "tag:node0:51372"],
		},
		{
			"src":  "tag:node0",
			"deny": ["tag:node1:22", "tag:node1:2049", "tag:node1:8017",
			         "tag:node1:6379", "tag:node1:51372"],
		},
	],
}
